00:00:05.086 --> 00:00:06.960
MARK MIRCHANDANI: The
Google Cloud Speech API

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.250
enables easy integration of
Google speech recognition

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.820
technologies into
developer applications.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.580
The Speech API allows you to
send audio, and receive a text

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.379
transcription from the service.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:18.120
Using the Google
Cloud Speech API,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.450
you can generate captions from a
video file, an audio recording,

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.890
or a live situation.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:25.740
The Speech API supports both
synchronous and asynchronous

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.637
speech-to-text transcription.

00:00:27.637 --> 00:00:29.970
Over on Qwiklabs, you'll be
diving into the Google Cloud

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.140
Speech API.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.840
In just 15 minutes,
you'll create an API key,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.789
create a Speech API request,
and call the Speech API request.

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:39.330
Like with all of
our Qwiklabs, you'll

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.680
have all the resources you
need to work on the lab.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.680
There are many applications
for this technology,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.680
and we'd love to hear
what you're doing with it.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.210
Let us know what you're up
to in the comments below.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.280
As you may already know,
this self-paced lab

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.966
is part of the baseline data,
ML and AI quest on Qwiklabs.

00:00:53.966 --> 00:00:55.590
Completing all of
the labs in the quest

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.880
earns you this badge to
recognize your new skills.

